      "content": "It's understandable to feel like you're fighting something predetermined, especially when you see patterns in your family history. While genetics play a role in how we experience the world, the human brain is also incredibly plastic, meaning it can change and adapt. Even if the foundation is set, the way you respond to it and the choices you make every day are still within your power.",
      "source": "target",
